Problem Statement
Create a Country class with the following attributes:
•	countryCode (String)
•	countryName (String)
•	population (long)
Then, write a Java program to:
1.	Store multiple Country objects in a TreeMap, where
o	key = countryCode
o	value = Country object
2.	Implement methods to:
o	Add a country
o	Remove a country
o	Search a country by countryCode
3.	Display all countries in sorted order of countryCode (TreeMap maintains natural sorting of keys).
Requirements
•	Use a TreeMap to automatically keep the entries sorted by countryCode.
•	Implement methods for:
o	addCountry()
o	removeCountry()
o	searchCountry()
o	displayAllCountries()
•	Use proper encapsulation in the Country class (private attributes with getters/setters).
•	Use a menu-driven approach for testing these operations (optional but recommended).
Hints
•	TreeMap automatically sorts keys in ascending order.
•	Use put() to add a key-value pair.
•	Use remove(key) to delete an entry.
•	Use containsKey(key) or get(key) for searching.
•	Override toString() in the Country class for easy display.




